<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chorni Klobuky</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Black Klobuks</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chorni Klobuky, 'Black Hats', were a union of Turkic nomad groups, including Torks, Berendei and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pechenegs">Pechenegs</a>, settled by the princes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a> along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ros-river">Ros River</a> south of the city in the 11th and 12th centuries. In return for land they served as frontier cavalry against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cumans">Cumans</a> and took part in the princes' wars. They disappeared as a distinct group after the Mongol invasion of 1240.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chorni-klobuky.jpg" alt="Chorni Klobuky" width="320" height="170" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1121_-_%D0%A2%D0%BE%D1%80%D0%BA%D0%B8_%D1%96_%D0%B1%D0%B5%D1%80%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%B4%D0%B5%D1%97_%D0%B2%D1%82%D1%96%D0%BA%D0%B0%D1%8E%D1%82%D1%8C_%D0%B7_%D0%A0%D1%83%D1%81%D1%96.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
